# Canonical byte-stable line endings.
#
# The F5 evidence contract binds two independent hashes to the same source:
#   * fitlab_evaluation.evidence.make_trust()  hashes GIT BLOB bytes
#   * fitlab_evaluation.run.identity()          hashes WORKING TREE bytes
# The workflow refuses to run unless those two agree exactly.
#
# With core.autocrlf=true and no .gitattributes, a fresh Windows checkout
# materialises CRLF working-tree files while the repository stores LF blobs.
# The two hash sets then disagree and every source file appears modified,
# which makes the F5 workflow refuse to start with SOURCE_NOT_FROZEN.
#
# Declaring text files as LF keeps the checkout byte-identical to the blob on
# every platform, so the source binding is reproducible anywhere.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary artifacts must never be line-ending converted.
*.gguf binary
*.zip binary
*.exe binary
*.dll binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.pdf binary
